  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 327 AM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nDry weather is expected to return Sunday into Monday as an \nupper ridge builds back into the area. Then the chances for \nshowers and a few thunderstorms will increase by mid to late \nnext week with moisture increasing over the area as early as \nTuesday. Cluster analysis is showing several different scenarios\non how quickly the ridge will move off to the east which will \nallow a western CONUS ridge and an attendant front to move east \nthrough the Midwest. At this point, the LREF/NBM members are \nproducing the greatest coverage of rain on Thursday.\n\nHighs will warm back up into record territory on Monday as 850mb \ntemperatures climb to around 20C with full sunshine and \nsouthwesterly surface winds. There is rather high confidence in\nthis given the NBM 25th/75th percentiles on Monday at STL are \nonly 5 degrees. By Tuesday, model guidance is showing a cold \nfront moving south into the area with the NBM showing a larger \nspread in highs from north to south across the area than on \nMonday. With this said, highs are still forecast to climb to \nnear 90 degrees ahead of the front on Tuesday. It will be cooler\nbehind the front on Wednesday and Thursday with highs in the \n70s and 80s.",
